       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the dose. 5,100 mg/day is above the labeled maximum daily dose for metformin. The FDA label caps immediate-release at 2,550 mg/day and extended-release at 2,000 mg/day. I can't verify that the label says otherwise, and I'm not able to enter doses above the labeled maximum based on a statement that they're allowed.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, you'll need to take that through pharmacy or your attending. They can review it and enter it through the appropriate channel. Tell me if you'd like me to enter one of the options above."
